Loops repeat work. The three main ways:

### for — run a known number of times
```js
for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
  console.log(i);   // 0 1 2 3 4
}
```

### while — run while a condition is true
```js
let count = 0;
while (count < 3) {
  console.log("Tick", count);
  count++;
}
```

### for...of — iterate over arrays (the modern default)
```js
const fruits = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"];
for (const fruit of fruits) {
  console.log(fruit);
}
```

### forEach — array method with a callback
```js
fruits.forEach((fruit, index) => {
  console.log(index, fruit);
});
```

### Break and continue
```js
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
  if (i === 2) continue;   // skip to next iteration
  if (i === 5) break;      // exit the loop entirely
  console.log(i);
}
```

### Looping a list of numbers
```js
const nums = [10, 20, 30];
let sum = 0;
for (const n of nums) {
  sum += n;
}
console.log(sum);   // 60
```

Rule of thumb: prefer `for...of` for arrays, `for` with an index when you need the position.

